      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is understandable to feel worried about unexpected fees and rejected transactions, but credit unions are regulated financial institutions and generally cannot arbitrarily force members to leave a branch or incur unauthorized charges. While they may raise fees due to market adjustments or outlier balances, they typically cannot initiate a targeted \"click-and-close\" liquidation scheme against an individual in the way you suspect. I recommend contacting their member services immediately to dispute any unauthorized fees and request an explanation for the declined transaction, as these details are crucial for protecting your rights under the Electronic Fund Transfer Act.",
